From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GIMPhoto scripts <gimphoto@localhost>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:03:46 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] Adjustment layers: Layer > New Adjustment Layer, applied to
 everything below

Photoshop's adjustment layers: a layer with no pixels of its own whose
adjustment (Curves, Levels, Hue-Saturation...) applies to everything
composited below it in its group, limited by its mask, opacity and blend
mode, editable again at any time, movable in the stack.

A new layer class, GimpAdjustmentLayer (app/core/gimpadjustmentlayer.[ch]),
is a GimpLayer whose source node is a pass-through with an "input" pad
instead of GIMP's buffer source: GimpDrawable links the layer's input (the
backdrop) to any source node that has one, so the layer's filter stack,
GIMP's own non-destructive filters, is applied to the backdrop and the
result is blended over it by the layer's mode node. The filter dialogs,
the effects rows under the layer, masks, opacity, modes, Merge Down (which
uses the real graph) and undo all work unchanged. The layer is created the
size of the canvas and stays so (gimpimage-resize.c resizes it whatever
the layer set says); its position is locked.

- app/actions/layers-actions.c, layers-commands.[ch]: Layer > New
  Adjustment Layer > one entry per GIMP colour filter, in Photoshop's
  order, then GIMP's own (Colorize, Color Temperature, Saturation,
  Shadows-Highlights). The layer goes above the selected layer (or at the
  top of a selected group), with a mask from the selection (which is then
  dropped, as in Photoshop) or a white one, and the filter's dialog opens on
  it. When the dialog is cancelled the layer is removed; when it is
  confirmed the mask becomes what is edited, so painting restricts the
  adjustment. A double click on an adjustment layer opens its adjustment
  again, like Photoshop's Properties panel.
- menus/image-menu.ui.in.in, menus/layers-menu.ui: the submenu, in the
  Layer menu and the Layers panel's right-click menu.
- app/xcf: PROP_GIMPHOTO_ADJUSTMENT_LAYER (1000, clear of GIMP's own
  properties) marks the layer in the XCF; GIMP without this patch opens the
  file with an empty layer carrying the filters (no visible adjustment).
- app/widgets/gimpviewrendererdrawable.c: the Layers panel shows the
  adjustment icon (gimphoto-adjustment-layer, from GIMPhoto's icons/) as
  the layer's thumbnail, as Photoshop does, instead of empty pixels.
- app/widgets/gimppropertieseditor.c: the Properties panel calls it an
  Adjustment Layer.

Test: Layer > New Adjustment Layer > Curves on a photo, bend the curve, OK:
the photo changes, the layer below does not; paint black on the mask to
limit it; drag the adjustment layer below the photo and it no longer
applies; Cancel in the dialog leaves no layer; save and reopen the XCF; Merge
Down bakes the curve into the photo.

